config BR2_PACKAGE_ADAU1451_FW
	bool "adau1451-fw (EA3 DSP firmware)"
	help
	  openHC's SigmaDSP firmware file for the EA3's ADAU1451, built
	  from board/ea/common/firmware/dsp/adau1451/ea3.json: the filter
	  tables behind every tone and EQ knob, the controls ALSA shows
	  for them, and the DSP's boot settings, all for stock's program,
	  as /lib/firmware/openhc/adau1451-ea3.bin. With a program
	  (below), also openHC's own: adau1451-ea3-openhc.bin, which the
	  board's device tree names and the adau1451-c4 codec driver
	  loads through the kernel's sigmadsp core.

	  Selected by the audio-dsp feature.

config BR2_PACKAGE_ADAU1451_FW_PROGRAM
	string "DSP program"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_ADAU1451_FW
	help
	  Folder holding openHC's DSP program as export2program.py
	  writes it: program.txt (memory blocks from a SigmaStudio+
	  export) and params.json (its parameter map). CI builds it in
	  the same run as the image (build.sh takes it from
	  OHC_DSP_PROGRAM); it is never committed. Set, the build also
	  makes /lib/firmware/openhc/adau1451-ea3-openhc.bin from
	  ea3-openhc.json: register init, program and parameters. Empty:
	  no file the device tree names, and the DSP is left as it
	  comes up.
